":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","color":"447744","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-09-09T15:02:04Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T23:57:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducable in v4.5.rc1.official [08e9e6b29]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.rc1 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7680) - AMD Ryzen 9 7900X3D 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 31.11 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I disable the user input while the game is embedded, and then turn off game embedding, user input will still not be accepted. This is confusing behaviour, as there is zero indication that user input has been disabled.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f376f4f3-bbcf-48cd-83b2-f1b0b3d0d363\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new project where you can detect user input (Fullscreen button for example)\n2. Start the game in embedded mode\n3. Switch from \"Input\" to \"2D\", for example.\n4. Stop the game\n5. Disable game embedding\n6. Start the game again\nNo user input will be detected.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110351/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110351/timeline","perfo